hoice.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the original example and locate the words or actions that support the idea. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Check your response against the feedback: did you address the same skill and show your reasoning? If a detail is uncertain, identify what would have to be checked. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than making the answer longer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Repeating the worked example cannot show transfer to new content. Correct the meaning, not just the appearance.","title":"Transfer to an independent example"}],"title":"Year 4, Week 33, Lesson 3: Noun groups","unit_number":7,"unit_title":"Folktales and world stories compared","week":33,"week_in_unit":3,"word_challenges":null,"worked_example":"WORK THROUGH THIS\n\"The approved classroom picture book\" = pointer + describers + thing. Expanding noun groups adds detail without a new sentence every time.\n\nExplain what makes this example accurate and effective, identifying its specific wording.","worked_visuals":[{"alt":"Building precise noun groups.","caption":"Detail without extra sentences.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Noun group</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">the approved picture book</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Parts</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">pointer + describers + thing</text></g></svg>"},{"alt":"Useful expansion vs cluttered contradicting words.","caption":"Use groups in a protocol paragraph.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" 